# Copy these values into the project's private .env, using the SMTP settings
# supplied by your mail provider. Do not edit this tracked example with secrets.
# Apply with make run. make mail-check checks TLS and login without
# sending mail; it does not prove delivery or DNS authentication.
NAFINITY_MAIL_FROM=support@example.com
NAFINITY_MAIL_PASSWORD='replace-with-the-provider-password'
NAFINITY_SMTP_HOST=smtp.your-provider.example
# Login defaults to MAIL_FROM and is shared with IMAP. Override once if needed:
#NAFINITY_MAIL_USER=your-mail-login
# Enable ordinary project notifications and emailed invitations:
#NAFINITY_MAIL_ENABLED=true
# For Mail-to-Ticket using the same mailbox, also configure:
#NAFINITY_IMAP_ENABLED=true
#NAFINITY_IMAP_HOST=imap.your-provider.example
#NAFINITY_MAIL_ACTOR=mailbot@example.com

# External SMTP uses STARTTLS/587. For implicit TLS add SMTP_PORT=465.
# A trusted local Postfix relay may use SMTP_SECURITY=none with SMTP_AUTH=off.
# Authentication without TLS is refused. LOGIN, PLAIN, CRAM-MD5 and XOAUTH2 are
# supported; OAuth token refresh remains the operator's responsibility.
# Separate SMTP_USER/PASSWORD or IMAP_USER/PASSWORD override shared credentials.
# Google: smtp.gmail.com, an approved sender and an app password if permitted:
# https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/185833
# Keep HOST empty for local Mailpit. All PHP settings live in app/src/config.php;
# no sendmail/msmtp config or additional mail server is required in the image.
# Account security mail uses the same sender and transport independently of
# the normal project-notification switch. Mail-to-Ticket confirmations use it too.
#
# Sending with your own domain also requires the provider's domain setup:
# - Verify the domain/sender with the provider; authenticate using its SMTP login.
# - In DNS, authorize the provider's sending servers in the domain's ONE SPF TXT
#   record. Extend an existing SPF record; never create a second v=spf1 record.
#   Use the provider's exact include/IP values. The app server's IP usually does
#   not belong there when delivery goes through the provider's SMTP relay.
# - Enable DKIM at the provider and publish its selector/key or CNAME in DNS.
# - Configure DMARC for the domain. The provider must preserve aligned MAIL FROM
#   or sign with aligned DKIM; providers may rewrite the return-path themselves.
# - Send to a real test inbox and inspect Authentication-Results for SPF, DKIM
#   and DMARC. Local Mailpit cannot prove internet delivery or authentication.
# SPF/DKIM/DMARC records cannot be generated or changed reliably from SMTP host
# and password alone. They depend on the provider, its domain-verification data,
# the existing DNS records and access to the operator's DNS account.
# References:
# https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7208
# https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9989
